# Page folders

When asked to **make a page** (or add a screen/route):

1. Create `src/pages/<slug>/index.tsx` — never a lone file like `src/pages/FooPage.tsx` at the pages root.
2. Prefer the folder name as the URL segment (`landing1` → `/landing1`).
3. Register the route in [`src/App.tsx`](src/App.tsx) importing from `@/pages/<slug>`.
4. Existing grouped areas (`catalog/`, `theme/`) already follow this pattern; extend those folders when adding related pages.

Landing variations: `landing` (default), `landing1`, `landing2`, `landing3` are independent copies under `src/pages/landing{,1,2,3}/`. Iterate on each folder separately. `/` redirects to `/landing`.
